      "text_raw": "The expression of the open-\nloop gain is given in this\nslide. Again, we find 4 poles\nand 3 zero’s. The GBW is\nthe same as for any three-\nstage amplifier. The second\nnon-dominant pole v coin-\n2\ncides with the first zero\nwhich occurs twice. One of\nthem is now cancelled out.\nThe other zero v will be\n2\nused to improve the phase\nmargin.\nThe right-hand zero v\n4\ncontains the GBW. This\nzero is always a lot higher\nthan the GBW, by factor k\nt\nand by the ratio’s C /C and g /g , which are both quite high. Indeed, compensation\nm2 2 m3 m1\ncapacitance C is always chosen larger than the parasitic node capacitance C .\nm2 2\nThis right-hand zero v is negligible.\n4\nThe stability conditions are discussed next.",
      "text": "The expression of the openloop gain is given in this slide. Again, we find 4 poles and 3 zero’s. The GBW is the same as for any threestage amplifier. The second non-dominant pole v coin- 2 cides with the first zero which occurs twice. One of them is now cancelled out. The other zero v will be 2 used to improve the phase margin. The right-hand zero v 4 contains the GBW. This zero is always a lot higher than the GBW, by factor k t and by the ratio’s C /C and g /g , which are both quite high. Indeed, compensation m2 2 m3 m1 capacitance C is always chosen larger than the parasitic node capacitance C . m2 2 This right-hand zero v is negligible. 4 The stability conditions are discussed next."
